AgentKit already supports Ollama, so you don't need to wait for a roadmap item. I can't speak to Inngest's future plans, but the practical answer is that it works today.

Ollama exposes an OpenAI-compatible API at `http://localhost:11434/v1`, or at your own internal host. AgentKit's `openai()` model helper accepts a custom `baseUrl`, so you can point it at Ollama:

```ts
import { createAgent, openai } from "@inngest/agent-kit";

const agent = createAgent({
  name: "local-agent",
  system: "You are a helpful assistant.",
  model: openai({
    model: "llama3.1",
    baseUrl: "http://your-ollama-host:11434/v1",
    apiKey: "ollama", // required by the client, ignored by Ollama
  }),
});
```

Use a model that supports tool calling if your agent uses tools. Quality varies a lot between local models.

For the data-residency requirement, you can also self-host the Inngest server, so orchestration and state stay in your own infrastructure. Your functions already run on your own compute. None of the provided sources cover this directly, so I'm going from my own knowledge of AgentKit. Please check the `baseUrl` option against the current AgentKit model docs before sending.

